    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71739869\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\"><p>As an advocate, one reads a lot of legal articles. These copies are of a wide variety; wordy and pretentious articles by veteran lawyers, inexperienced articles by students with a staccato logical flow, and of course, a great number of absolutely brilliant articles. However, more recently, one has come across whole clusters of articles which share the same soulless dullness which makes them unreadable. While they often promise to make interesting points, they are so unreadable, one’s eye drifts off after the first few paragraphs. This is the scourge of legal academia today. With so many AI tools at everyone’s fingertips, each of us can produce high volumes of writing that appear to be scholarly with minimal effort.</p><p>Welcome to the era of ‘AI slop’. AI slop is a slang-term for low-quality, high-volume digital content produced by AI. It is the result of humans delegating their thinking and writing process to AI models, which leads to the slow evaporation of creativity from academic thought.</p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- November 25, 2026 01:00 am IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71739869\" data-title=\"The scourge of legal academia\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/op-ed/the-scourge-of-legal-academia/article71739869.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-5755ed462ae8fce44b2ea991-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/op-ed/the-